StyxWire README
===============

StyxWire is a network tool that sends custom TCP/IP packets and displays
target replies, the way ping does with ICMP. It handles fragmentation and
almost arbitrary packet size and content from the command line, and it
embeds a Tcl scripting engine and the APD packet description language for
building and dissecting packets programmatically.

It is the continuation of hping3 by Salvatore Sanfilippo. The command
line, the exit codes, the Tcl API and the APD language are kept
compatible; the binary is installed as "styxwire" with "hping3", "hping2"
and "hping" as symbolic links, so existing scripts keep working.

WHAT IT IS USED FOR

	- Firewall and ACL testing
	- Advanced/port scanning (--scan)
	- Network performance tests with different protocols, sizes,
	  TOS and fragmentation
	- Path MTU discovery
	- Traceroute over arbitrary protocols
	- Remote OS fingerprinting and TCP/IP stack auditing
	- Teaching and learning TCP/IP

	Sending and capturing packets needs root (raw sockets), and the
	command line sends IPv4 only; building and dissecting do not
	need root and handle IPv6 as well (docs/IPV6.txt). --dry-run (build and print packets),
	--read file.pcap (dissect a savefile) and the offline Tcl commands
	(styxwire build/describe/validate) run as an ordinary user.

	--json makes styxwire emit newline-delimited JSON events on stdout
	(replies, ICMP errors, statistics) with diagnostics on stderr, for
	pipelines and automation; see docs/JSON.txt.

BUILDING AND TESTING

	$ ./configure          (./configure --help lists the options)
	$ make
	$ make check           offline test-suite: no root, no traffic
	# make install         or: make install DESTDIR=/some/stage

	$ make bench           offline benchmark of the packet engine

	See INSTALL for the details (Tcl on/off, staged installation,
	sanitizer builds, fuzzing, benchmarking, cross compiling). The
	development reports for this tree are docs/ASAMA1-RAPORU.md
	through docs/ASAMA5-RAPORU.md; the design decisions are in
	docs/KARAR-KAYITLARI.md (all in Turkish).

SCRIPTING

	Run an example script from the lib directory with:

		styxwire exec ScriptName.htcl <arguments, if required>

	The Tcl API is documented in docs/API.txt, the APD packet
	description language in docs/APD.txt, what does and does not
	work for IPv6 in docs/IPV6.txt, and the supported platforms and
	link-layer types in docs/PLATFORMS.txt. The startup file is
	~/.styxwirerc (falling back to ~/.hpingrc); STYXWIRE_NORC disables
	it and STYXWIRE_RC=path selects a specific one.

REQUIREMENTS

	A supported unix-like OS (Linux is the tested one), a C compiler,
	GNU make, libpcap with headers. Tcl 8.6 or 9 (with headers) is
	optional but strongly suggested.

CREDITS

	StyxWire builds on hping3 by Salvatore Sanfilippo (antirez) and
	the many contributors listed in the AUTHORS file. The original
	hping site was http://www.hping.org.

